Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: parser.c
Line: 10880
Function: xmlParseTryOrFinish
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In state XML_PARSER_XML_DECL, after seeing "<?", the code unconditionally reads input->cur[2..5] to match "xml ". Availability is only ensured to be >= 2 (or that "?>" exists somewhere). With short buffers like "<?x?>" (length 5), xmlParseLookupString finds "?>", but input->cur[5] is out of bounds, causing an out-of-bounds read.

